{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["And fire came forth from before YHWH — from the Holy of Holies by way of the golden altar, to offer the incense, which is prior to the offering of the tamid, as it says in tractate Yoma. And there it found Aharon's sons by the golden altar and consumed them; and afterward it went forth and came upon the outer altar, ותאכל על המזבח את העולה ואת השלמים."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Rashbam appears to link the fire of Lev 9:24 with the later death of Aharon's sons (Lev 10:2); the referent of 'found Aharon's sons' and 'consumed them' follows this midrashic reading cited from Yoma. The phrase ושרפם rendered 'consumed them'; ואח\"כ expanded as 'and afterward.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:29.909140523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}